    "Reason : 1 - On 11 September 2025 the proposed use of the existing building's ground floor premises as a caf�/ restaurant and hot food takeaway use for the sale of food and drink for consumption within and outside of the premises (Sui Generis) was not lawful, contrary to Section 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) and Schedule 2, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe proposed mixed caf�/ restaurant and hot food takeaway use of the existing building's ground floor premises would be a Sui Generis use, rather than a Commercial, Business and Service (Class E) use, as established by Article 3 and Schedule 2, Part A of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended) and consequently the permitted development right for the change of use of existing hot food takeaways (Sui Generis) to caf�/ restaurants and hot food takeaways (Sui Generis) would not apply to the site.  "
